---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms | UI Forge" description="The UI Forge terms of use.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: August 31, 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-base leading-8 text-zinc-400">
      <section><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Using UI Forge</h2><p class="mt-3">You may copy, modify, and use the published components in personal and commercial projects. You are responsible for reviewing the source and adapting it to your application's needs.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Provided as-is</h2><p class="mt-3">UI Forge is provided as-is without warranties of any kind. We do not guarantee that every component will work in every environment or meet a particular performance, accessibility, or security requirement.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Your responsibility</h2><p class="mt-3">Before shipping, test the components in your application, review dependencies, and ensure your use complies with applicable laws and the licenses of any third-party code.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Changes</h2><p class="mt-3">These terms may be updated as the project evolves. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept the revised terms.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
